---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="IUT de Figeac"
  category="Education | Mechanical & Production Engineering"
  year="2021 | 2024"
  description="Bachelor of Technology in Mechanical and Production Engineering at IUT de Figeac."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    Three-year technical degree focused on mechanical design,
    manufacturing, industrialisation and production engineering |
    providing a strong foundation for advanced engineering studies.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | Programme
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        A strong technical foundation.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I completed a Bachelor of Technology in Mechanical
        and Production Engineering at IUT de Figeac.
      </p>

      <p>
        The programme combined mechanical design,
        manufacturing processes, industrialisation,
        production methods and engineering analysis.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Main Fields
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        From design to manufacturing.
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Mechanical design</li>
        <li>CAD modelling</li>
        <li>Manufacturing processes</li>
        <li>Machining</li>
        <li>Industrialisation</li>
        <li>Production engineering</li>
        <li>Materials and mechanical behaviour</li>
        <li>Metrology and quality control</li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | Engineering Approach
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Understanding how parts are really produced.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The programme helped me connect design decisions
        with manufacturing constraints.
      </p>

      <p>
        This experience remains particularly valuable in my current work |
        allowing me to approach mechanical design with a strong awareness
        of machining, assembly, tolerancing and industrial feasibility.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | Industrial Experience
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        First experience in the aerospace industry.
      </h2>

      <p>
        During the programme, I completed an internship at Ratier-Figeac,
        working in an industrial aerospace environment.
      </p>

      <p>
        The internship focused on industrial cleaning processes
        and REACH-related considerations, giving me early exposure
        to industrial constraints, process control and regulated environments.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | Skills Developed
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Building practical engineering skills.
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Mechanical design methodology</li>
        <li>Technical drawing</li>
        <li>Manufacturing process selection</li>
        <li>Machining fundamentals</li>
        <li>Dimensional tolerancing</li>
        <li>Industrial problem solving</li>
        <li>Production organisation</li>
        <li>Technical communication</li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      06 | Progression
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        From technical engineering to broader system design.
      </h2>

      <p>
        This degree gave me the practical and technical foundation
        required to continue toward an engineering degree at ICAM.
      </p>

      <p>
        It also shaped my interest in machine tools,
        mechanical systems and the relationship between
        design, manufacturing and industrial performance.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>